  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 7901.02 Scope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7901.02 Scope.\n\n(a) The missing adult program shall apply to situations when a person, who is 18 years of age or older and who resides or is believed to be in New Hampshire, is reported missing, and a law enforcement agency determine that the person meets one of the categories listed in RSA 106-J:1, IV.\n\n(b) The rules are not intended to remove the discretion of a law enforcement agency to notify the National Crime Information Center (NCIC) when an adult is missing under circumstances other than those specified in RSA 106-J:1, IV, when the law enforcement agency has reasonable concern for such adult's safety.\n\nSource. #14199, eff 2-25-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c7900.html"
